| `make exit-codes-sh` `[tree]` | Regenerates the shell helper `scripts/exit_codes.sh` from `scripts/exit_codes.py`; a second run writes nothing. | `make exit-codes-sh` | — | Writes the tree; `make check-exit-codes` is the gate. Writes the helper whatever `shell.enabled` says. Not the gate that holds a shell script to the helper: `tests/integration/test_exit_gate.py` is. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md) | always |
